          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "warning",
          "guid": "mry8pv8ikzh94td8",
          "message": {
            "text": "Fail-soft had a hole: a subprocess that starts but never exits.\n\nEvery error path here resolves null so a broken renderer degrades to the code block — except the one where the child neither errors nor closes. There the promise stayed pending forever, and whatever awaited it (the /file/:id render) hung with it. That is strictly worse than the fallback: a visible \"no diagram\" beats a request that never returns.\n\nFound by accident. A restricted environment blocked Chromium from launching in a way that wedged the child rather than failing it, and the unit test died on vitest's timeout instead of fail-softing — which is what a real user would have seen as a hung page.\n\nThe timer is unref()d so a pending render never keeps the process alive on its own, and cleared in finish so a normal close does not leave a stray kill armed. timeoutMs is injectable purely so the regression test can drive the path in 200 ms instead of 30 s; nothing in production passes it.\n\nThe same fix is in plugins/plantuml/src/index.ts — identical shape, java instead of a browser.",
            "markdown": "Fail-soft had a hole: a subprocess that starts but never exits.\n\nEvery error path here resolves `null` so a broken renderer degrades to the code block — except the one where the child neither errors nor closes. There the promise stayed pending forever, and whatever awaited it (the `/file/:id` render) hung with it. That is strictly worse than the fallback: a visible \"no diagram\" beats a request that never returns.\n\nFound by accident. A restricted environment blocked Chromium from launching in a way that wedged the child rather than failing it, and the unit test died on vitest's timeout instead of fail-softing — which is what a real user would have seen as a hung page.\n\nThe timer is `unref()`d so a pending render never keeps the process alive on its own, and cleared in `finish` so a normal close does not leave a stray kill armed. `timeoutMs` is injectable purely so the regression test can drive the path in 200 ms instead of 30 s; nothing in production passes it.\n\nThe same fix is in `plugins/plantuml/src/index.ts` — identical shape, `java` instead of a browser."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "plugins/mermaid/src/index.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 59,
                  "endLine": 70,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "/** Wall-clock ceiling on one render. A headless browser that never exits would\n *  otherwise leave the promise pending forever, hanging the request that awaits\n *  it — a worse failure than the code-block fallback this degrades to. Generous\n *  enough for a cold Chromium start on a loaded machine. */\nexport const RENDER_TIMEOUT_MS = 30_000;\n\nexport function renderMermaid(source: string, cli: string = mmdcCli(), opts: { timeoutMs?: number } = {}): Promise<string | null> {\n  if (source.trim() === '' || !existsSync(cli)) return Promise.resolve(null);\n  return new Promise((resolve) => {\n    let done = false;\n    let workDir: string | null = null;\n    let timer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined;"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
